This test ensures that cross-file CSS extraction deduplicates identical rules.

When two files both use [%css "display: flex"] and [%css "color: blue"], the
generated CSS should contain each rule only once, while preserving rules
unique to each file.

  $ refmt --parse re --print ml input_a.re > output_a.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl output_a.ml -o output_a.ml
  $ refmt --parse re --print ml input_b.re > output_b.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl output_b.ml -o output_b.ml
  $ styled-ppx.generate output_a.ml output_b.ml > styles.css
  $ cat styles.css
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  ._a_5r08qs,._t1_5r08qs:not(x-),._t2_5r08qs:not(x-):not(x-){display:flex;}
  ._a_4esm7b,._t1_4esm7b:not(x-),._t2_4esm7b:not(x-):not(x-){color:blue;}
  ._a_7peacs,._t1_7peacs:not(x-),._t2_7peacs:not(x-):not(x-){margin:10px;}
  ._a_94xp1v,._t1_94xp1v:not(x-),._t2_94xp1v:not(x-):not(x-){padding:20px;}
